  "notes": "{主導|しゅどう} means taking the lead in directing an activity or process. It emphasizes active guidance rather than mere authority.\n\nWORD FORMATION:\n{主|しゅ} (main) + {導|どう} (lead, guide)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ～{主導|しゅどう}の: led by ~, ~-led\n- {主導|しゅどう}{権|けん}: initiative, leadership (the right to lead)\n- {主導|しゅどう}{権|けん}を{握|にぎ}る: to seize the initiative\n- ～が{主導|しゅどう}する: to take the lead in\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {指導|しどう}: instruction, guidance (teaching-oriented)\n- {率先|そっせん}: taking the initiative (emphasizes being first to act)\n- リーダーシップ: leadership (general, loanword)\n\nREGISTER:\nUsed frequently in news, business, and political contexts. Formal in tone.",
